OL,3,ATourism tax needs to be more flexible
OL,4,Ain Wales, warns expert
OL,5,
OL,6,FWales' tourism tax needs to be more
OL,7,Fflexible, an expert has said.
OL,9,FLast week, Anglesey council rejected
OL,10,Fintroducing the visitor levy for now,
OL,11,Fover concerns for its tourism industry,
OL,12,Fwhile Gwynedd and Conwy councils both
OL,13,Fpostponed making any decision on the
OL,14,Fnightly fee.
OL,16,FIt is down to local authorities to
OL,17,Fdecide whether they want to introduce
OL,18,Fthe Welsh government legislation -
OL,19,Fmeaning from 2027 a fixed price can be
OL,20,Fcharged per person, per night - and
OL,21,Fapplies to both adults and children.
OL,23,APub: 27-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  BusinessC Nat TVF  Nat News
